31,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Good morning, everyone. I hope you all rested well. As we begin today, I find myself reflecting on our silence. I wonder, does a quiet nature stem from a peaceful heart or a hidden agenda?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a profound question, Servas. I believe silence can be a sanctuary for thought. However, I understand why it might seem suspicious to some. I am simply observing the flow of our words.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,1,1,talk,Yumi,,"Good morning! I'm a little sad that we have to start suspecting each other already, but I'll try my best! @Jonathan, you seem so thoughtful, so I trust your observations! What do you all think?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Yumi, trust without verification is a liability. @Servas, silence is indeed a tool for deception. We should examine who has been the most reserved or deflective, as they may be hiding their true identity.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,1,1,talk,May,,"@Victoria, still with the lectures! You're so focused on ""verification"" that you're ignoring the obvious. Look at Jonathan and Servas—they're being so vague and ""thoughtful."" Isn't that the perfect cover for a wolf?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Jonathan"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, it is natural to mistake composure for evasion. However, haste often leads to error. I believe we should look for those who react with aggression when questioned, as fear often masks itself as anger.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, I understand your suspicion, but aggression can also be a mask. I prefer to remain calm to ensure my judgment is clear. Perhaps we should consider if those pushing for quick accusations are trying to divert our attention.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,1,2,talk,Yumi,,"Oh, wow, everyone is getting so serious! @May, @Jonathan, please don't fight! I don't want anyone to be angry. Maybe we should just listen to each other more? I'm starting to feel a bit confused!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Yumi, confusion is a result of prioritizing emotion over analysis. @May, your attempt to deflect suspicion toward the calmest players is a common tactic to create chaos. We must focus on the facts, not the noise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,1,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, you're so predictable! ""Facts,"" ""noise,"" ""analysis""—you're just using big words to sound superior. It's almost pathetic. Why are you so desperate to shut me down? Are you afraid I'll actually find the wolf?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, @Victoria, please. This cycle of hostility only serves the wolf by blinding us. Let us look at the patterns: who benefits from this discord? A calm heart sees the truth more clearly than a stormy one.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Servas. The friction between May and Victoria is distracting us from the actual goal. While we debate personalities, the wolf remains hidden. Perhaps we should ask ourselves who truly benefits from this chaos.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""May"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,1,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Servas, @Jonathan, you're both so right! The fighting is making me really sad. I think we should all try to be friends again so we can think clearly! Who do you think is being the most honest?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Yumi, honesty is not a feeling, but a consistency of facts. @May, your aggression is not a sign of passion, but a pattern of deflection. I have a rational basis for my suspicions, and I will not be swayed by noise.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,1,3,talk,May,,"@Victoria, you're so obsessed with your ""rational basis"" that you've become a robot. It's actually scary. @Yumi, honey, don't let her scare you. Isn't it weird how Victoria just loves pointing fingers at me? It's a classic diversion!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,1,4,talk,Servas,,"@May, @Victoria, your clash has become a veil. When two people fight, the one who truly hides often watches from the sidelines. Let us consider if this discord is a calculated distraction. Who among us is too quiet?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a delicate balance. While the conflict is distracting, being too quiet can indeed be seen as a strategy. However, we must be careful not to mistake a peaceful nature for a hidden agenda.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,1,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm really worried now! @Servas and @Jonathan are both saying that being quiet or fighting could be a trick. I don't know who to believe! Does anyone have a clue who the werewolf is? Please help me!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
